From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: keep vdev usable when PPE attach fails

PPE direct switching is an optional acceleration path. A transient PPE
resource or firmware error must not tear down an otherwise valid AP/STA
vdev; doing so makes every client fail to associate when the accelerator is
busy.
Leave the vdev on the normal ath12k datapath and report the error for
diagnostics. A later wireless reload can retry PPE attachment.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -11131,3 +11131,3 @@
-		ath12k_mac_vdev_stop(arvif);
-		arvif->is_started = false;
-		return ret;
+		/* Drop a stale/partially programmed endpoint before fallback. */
+		ath12k_ppe_ds_vif_detach(arvif);
+		/* PPE is acceleration only; keep the normal vdev datapath. */
@@ -11620,3 +11620,4 @@
-		ath12k_mac_vdev_stop(arvif);
-		arvif->is_started = false;
-		goto out;
+		/* Drop a stale/partially programmed endpoint before fallback. */
+		ath12k_ppe_ds_vif_detach(arvif);
+		/* PPE is acceleration only; keep the normal vdev datapath. */
+		ret = 0;
